{"title":"Special right triangles","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>A <b>special right triangle</b> is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Right_triangle\" title=\"Right triangle\">right triangle</a> whose angles and ratios of sides make the triangle useful.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"45-45-90_Triangles\">45-45-90 Triangles</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Special_right_triangles&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: 45-45-90 Triangles\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<dl><dd><i>Main article: <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=45-45-90_triangle\" title=\"45-45-90 triangle\">45-45-90 triangle</a></i></dd></dl>\n<p>A 45-45-90 triangle is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Right_triangle\" title=\"Right triangle\">right triangle</a> that has two <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/d/8adb649f063149ebc97d3ee58c4fd38d4c440846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> angles. All 45-45-90 triangles are <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Isosceles\" title=\"Isosceles\">isosceles</a>, so let's call both legs of the triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. If that is the case, then the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Hypotenuse\" title=\"Hypotenuse\">hypotenuse</a> will always be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/a/73a52af2773f6848e741bb2669ddfae8330ceb88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\sqrt2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"30-60-90_Triangles\">30-60-90 Triangles</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Special_right_triangles&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: 30-60-90 Triangles\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<dl><dd><i>Main article: <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=30-60-90_triangle\" title=\"30-60-90 triangle\">30-60-90 triangle</a></i></dd></dl>\n<p>A 30-60-90 triangle is a right triangle that has a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/9/919bf5d461970fc8d905d63704ef763c08594184.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30^\\circ$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" /> angle and a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/f/29fa0a9949f018e121b2093216dd5db13d3abef0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> angle. Let's call the side opposite of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/9/919bf5d461970fc8d905d63704ef763c08594184.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30^\\circ$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" /> angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. Then, the side opposite of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/f/29fa0a9949f018e121b2093216dd5db13d3abef0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> angle would have a length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/3/f936a86130212e5ec45bd13dd6a571b9695bc4a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\sqrt 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" />. Finally, the hypotenuse of a 30-60-90 Triangle would have a length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/c/2ec701493fa72dda5d6747fe14f30e7b1c2fb6c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />. There is also the ratio of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/4/ae47591003e4756514fc8bc7800936d87e0dc82d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1:\\sqrt3:2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"75\" height=\"21\" />. With 2 as the hypotenuse and 1 opposite of the 30 degrees. That leaves <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/9/c99f089046b752269e77100c333b11d8d72e5895.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"26\" height=\"21\" /> as the only length left.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Special_right_triangles&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_triple\" title=\"Pythagorean triple\">Pythagorean triple</a></li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Special_right_triangles&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018110813\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.022 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.042 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 99/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 478/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 104/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 5/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2031/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   18.373      1 -total\n 56.02%   10.292      2 Template:Main\n 31.35%    5.760      1 Template:Stub\n 26.80%    4.923      2 Template:Hatnote\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:30744:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018110813 and revision id 241494. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}